sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Train as Training Loop
    participant Model as NeuralNetwork.forward()
    participant Flat as Flatten
    participant L1 as Linear 784 to 512
    participant R1 as ReLU 1
    participant L2 as Linear 512 to 512
    participant R2 as ReLU 2
    participant L3 as Linear 512 to 10

    Note over Train,L3: B = current batch size (up to 64)
    Train->>Model: X with shape [B, 1, 28, 28]
    Model->>Flat: Flatten image dimensions
    Flat-->>Model: [B, 784]

    Model->>L1: Apply learned weights and bias
    L1-->>Model: [B, 512]
    Model->>R1: max(0, x)
    R1-->>Model: [B, 512]

    Model->>L2: Apply learned weights and bias
    L2-->>Model: [B, 512]
    Model->>R2: max(0, x)
    R2-->>Model: [B, 512]

    Model->>L3: Apply learned weights and bias
    L3-->>Model: Logits [B, 10]
    Model-->>Train: Raw scores for 10 clothing classes
    Note over Train,Model: Logits go directly to CrossEntropyLoss<br/>No explicit softmax layer
